      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bracey sits on the abandoned CSX Norlina Subdivision, a line that ran until the 1980s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracey%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A ferry across the Roanoke River in 1762 sparked a small riverside community that would become Bracey.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://braceyvirginia.com/bracey-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bracey is the closest access point to Lake Gaston from Interstate‑85, making it a gateway to the lake’s four quadrants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracey%2C_Virginia",
